# uscasestatus.com — Cursor Rules

## Project overview
A USCIS immigration case tracker at uscasestatus.com. Users enter a USCIS receipt number and get:
- Real-time case status pulled from the public USCIS case status endpoint
- Plain-English explanation of what their status means
- Case history timeline
- Processing time comparison
- Email / WhatsApp / web push alerts when their status changes
- A dashboard to save and manage multiple cases
- Bilingual (English + Spanish)

## Tech stack
- Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Supabase (PostgreSQL database + Auth via magic link)
- Resend (transactional email)
- Upstash Redis (caching + rate limiting)
- Vercel (hosting + cron jobs for polling)
- Recharts (charts)
- next-intl (i18n for EN/ES)

## Design system
- Primary color: teal #0F6E56 (light fill #E1F5EE, dark text #085041)
- Background: #FAFAFA (off-white)
- Status colors: amber for pending, green for approved, red for denied/RFE
- Font: Inter (via next/font)
- Border radius: 8px (md), 12px (lg for cards)
- Borders: 0.5px, very subtle
- No gradients, no drop shadows, flat and clean

## File structure conventions
- /app — Next.js App Router pages and layouts
- /app/api — API routes (server-side only)
- /components — Reusable React components
- /lib — Utilities, Supabase client, USCIS polling logic
- /data — Static JSON files (status explanations, processing times, form metadata)
- /public — Static assets

## Key data files
- /data/status-explanations.json — maps every USCIS status message to plain_english, what_to_do, is_positive
- /data/processing-times.json — USCIS published processing times by form + service center
- /data/forms.json — metadata for all 15 tracked form types

## API conventions
- All API routes in /app/api/[route]/route.ts
- Always return { data, error } shape
- Use Supabase service role client for server-side routes
- Rate limit all public routes with Upstash Redis

## Receipt number formats
Valid USCIS receipt number prefixes: IOE, WAC, EAC, LIN, SRC, YSC, ZAR, ZCH, ZHN, NBC, MSC, MGL, MCT
Format: 3-letter prefix + 10 digits = 13 characters total
Example: IOE0912345678 or WAC2190012345

## USCIS Case Status API (official Torch API)
Legacy HTML scraping (mycasestatus.do) is dead — Cloudflare blocks it.
Use the official Case Status API with OAuth 2.0 client credentials:

- Sandbox base: https://api-int.uscis.gov
- Production base: https://api.uscis.gov
- Token: POST /oauth/accesstoken (grant_type=client_credentials)
- Case: GET /case-status/{receiptNumber} with Authorization: Bearer {token}
- Env: USCIS_CLIENT_ID, USCIS_CLIENT_SECRET, USCIS_API_BASE (optional; defaults to sandbox)
- When credentials are missing, lib/uscis falls back to deterministic mock fixtures for local UI work
- Tokens expire ~30 minutes — cache and refresh server-side only; never expose credentials to the client

## Supabase schema
- cases: id, receipt, form_type, last_status, last_checked, history (jsonb), created_at
- alerts: id, receipt, email, phone, channels (jsonb), confirmed, user_id (nullable), created_at
- lookups: id, receipt_block, form_type, status_slug, status_text, prefix, checked_at (anonymized corpus)
- users: managed by Supabase Auth

## Coding style
- Always use TypeScript with proper types, no any
- Use server components by default, add use client only when needed
- Tailwind classes only — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- Always handle loading and error states in components
- Mobile-first: write mobile styles first, use md: and lg: prefixes for larger screens